---
description: Infrastructure and IaC rules (Terraform, pipelines, deploy artifacts)
globs: ["infra/**", "ops/**", "deploy/**", "**/*.tf", "**/*.tfvars", "**/*.yaml", "**/*.yml", "**/Dockerfile", "**/docker-compose*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yml"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Run format/validation before merge (e.g., `terraform fmt`/`validate`, linting workflows).
- Never hardcode secrets; rely on secret managers/CI secrets and minimal scopes.
- Use least-privilege IAM and scoped access tokens; document rationale for elevated roles.
- Name resources predictably and tag with owner, environment, and purpose.
- Keep changes backward-compatible and roll out with plans/previews; prefer staged rollouts.
- Add health checks and readiness probes; fail fast on unhealthy deployments.
- Record runbooks for new services; include rollback/cleanup steps.
